hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24181","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted the herdsmen to cast a day and leave a day."
"24182","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adiyy, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted the camel herdsmen in staying overnight away from Mina: they cast on the day of sacrifice, then cast the morrow or after the morrow, the two days, then cast on the day of departure."
"24183","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adiyy, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted the camel herdsmen in staying overnight to cast on the day of sacrifice, then gather the casting of two days after sacrifice and cast it in one of them. Malik said: I thought in the last of them, then they cast on the day of departure."
"24184","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr informed me, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from Asim ibn Adiyy, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted the herdsmen to take turns: they cast on the day of sacrifice, then leave a day and a night, then cast the morrow."
